#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:132
#: ca7093fbb04a4b129196205afba31b62
msgid ""
"Set ``backup_id`` to the value in the last line of ``backup-header``. (Note "
"that there is a hyphen in ``backup-id`` in the file, whereas there is an "
"underscore in ``backup_id`` in the variable you’re setting.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:140
#: 0d0e121dd90f4679bd3e64326ebd2643
msgid "Verify and decrypt, decompress, and extract the ``qubes.xml`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:150
#: 2a6a329b27a246cabafb6034096ab226
msgid ""
"If this pipeline fails, it is likely that the backup is corrupted or has "
"been tampered with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:152
#: 766c75c94aa241f884914ca11f9571ff
msgid ""
"**Note:** If your backup was compressed with a program other than ``gzip``, "
"you must substitute the correct compression program in the command above. "
"This information is contained in ``backup-header`` (see step 4). For "
"example, if your backup is compressed with ``bzip2``, use ``bzip2 -d`` "
"instead of ``gzip -d`` in the command above. You might need to install a "
"package of the same name (in this example, ``bzip2``) through your "
"distribution’s package manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:156
#: 251edf5ea5f144109fef648e550c5202
msgid ""
"Search inside of the ``qubes.xml`` file for the ``backup-path`` of the qube "
"whose data you wish to restore. If you install the ``xmlstarlet`` package, "
"the following command will convert ``qubes.xml`` to a friendlier listing for "
"this purpose:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:183
#: 01874443ff56452495f48e00c499a316
msgid ""
"The example output above shows that the backup file includes a qube named "
"``personal`` and a qube named ``vault``, with ``backup-path`` values of "
"``vm123/`` and ``vm321/`` respectively. (Every other listed qube was not "
"selected to be included in the backup file.) Use the corresponding value to "
"untar the necessary data files of the qube:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:191
#: ccf217d06ac745fb8797d4cb891d4d0c
msgid "Verify and decrypt the backed up data, decompress it, and extract it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:202
#: d6c87237c8484747a95c8e57c0339caa
msgid ""
"If this pipeline fails, it is likely that the backup is corrupted or has "
"been tampered with. Also see the note in step 6 about substituting a "
"different compression program for ``gzip``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:205
#: bd039fca71644a468cf3627ea687dc9b
msgid "Mount ``private.img`` and access your data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:207
#: 53eee266ead343d2af317e1044731b48
msgid ""
"Beside the security risk of accessing compromised *files*,  there can be "
"security consequences of simply mounting *file systems* if an attacker had "
"been able to compromise the file system in some way. For better security, "
"handle these files within an isolated environment like a dedicated VM, a "
"Live USB, or by using `libguestfs <https://libguestfs.org/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:222
